Pace & Pulse — change log
=========================
Newest first. One entry per published version (the number shown at the bottom of every page).
Each entry says what changed and why. Algorithm changes name the old and new algorithm ids.

v5 — 2026-10-05
  Every measurement is now its own versioned algorithm in src/algo/ (one file each):
    VO2alg2 (VO₂max), HRMAXalg2 (max heart rate), LOADalg1 (TRIMP), ZONEalg1 (HR zones & intensity mix),
    FFalg1 (fitness/fatigue/form), ACWRalg1 (7-day load range), ENDalg1 (endurance score),
    DRIFTalg2 (HR drift), BESTalg2 (best & race-like efforts), RACEalg1 (race predictions),
    EFalg1 (aerobic efficiency), GAPalg1 (grade-adjusted pace).
    Why: so each calculation is defined in one place and can be improved as a new version (alg3, alg4…)
    with a written reason, instead of edits scattered through core.js.
  Every place a measurement appears (tiles, chart titles, workout stats, tables, Profile) is now tappable:
    it opens how the number is calculated, the formula, its inputs and limits, the current algorithm id
    and its version history. Profile → "How the numbers are made" lists all algorithms.
  Numbers are unchanged: the sample athlete's results were compared value-for-value before and after the split.
  Added this change.log. Why: keep a trace of every update and the reason for it.

v4 — 2026-10-05
  VO2alg1 → VO2alg2. Why: VO2alg1 regressed Daniels' curved oxygen cost directly on heart rate, which
    read 3–8 ml/kg/min too low on easy runs (a true 35 showed as 28–32 — the "29" seen in the chart).
    VO2alg2 regresses grade-adjusted speed on heart rate, anchored at (resting HR, 0), extends it to max HR
    to get the speed at VO₂max, then converts with Daniels' cost. Tested unbiased (±0.2) at VO₂max 35–55.
  BESTalg1 → BESTalg2. Why: tempo runs at 88% HRmax counted as "races" and pulled VO₂max down. Race-like
    efforts now need the heart rate an all-out effort of that length needs; times are scaled to the exact
    distance. Races fade out of VO₂max over 60 days instead of dropping off at day 60.
  DRIFTalg1 → DRIFTalg2. Why: drift on interval sessions is meaningless; unsteady runs are now skipped.
  HRMAXalg1 → HRMAXalg2. Why: one optical-sensor spike could set max HR; also like Garmin the age estimate
    is now a floor because most training never reaches true max.
  Charts: tick labels get enough decimals to never repeat (fixes "29 | 29 | 29"); minimum y-ranges so
    small wobbles don't look like big swings; lines clipped to the plot; shaded areas no longer bridge gaps;
    bar width capped; axis margin sized to its labels; monthly table divide-by-zero fixed.
  New look: dark "Volt" theme by default plus Ember, Glacier, Ultraviolet, Daylight and Match device; font
    style and text size settings (Profile → Appearance). Chart colours checked for colour-blind safety.
  Overview became a customizable dashboard: add, remove, resize and reorder cards (new: This week, Training
    load range, Activity calendar, Intensity mix, Personal bests, Fitness & fatigue, Endurance and
    Efficiency charts).
  AI coach with Google Gemini (key stays on the device): 4-line read on the overview and an opinion per workout.

v3 — 2026-10-05
  Version number and build time shown at the bottom of every page, stamped by build.sh.
  Why: to be sure the published page is the latest version.

v2 — 2026-10-05
  Online accounts (Firebase) as an opt-in: "Save account online" copies the on-device profile and workouts.
  Private share links for profile, workouts and chart images; a feed to publish workouts (name, time,
  distance, optional heart rate and route) with follow. Multi-file and folder import; the file picker no
  longer filters by extension so phones can select .fit files.
  Why: sync across devices and share progress, while keeping profiles private by default.

v1 — 2026-10-05
  First version: Garmin FIT/TCX/GPX/ZIP/CSV import, VO₂max (VO2alg1), endurance score, training load,
  trends, records, maps, local profiles.
